Provenance and independence
---------------------------
ecotrajpy was written by AI coding agents (OpenAI Codex and Anthropic Claude
Code) working from the published papers and the public ecotraj documentation
(help pages and vignettes). It is an independent implementation: no source
code from the R package ecotraj was copied or translated, and the agents
worked under a written rule not to read it (docs/API_SPEC.md).

The R package ecotraj (GPL >= 2) was used only as an external reference to
benchmark numerical outputs, run as a separate program (Rscript). Where
ecotraj's outputs on edge cases (for example row order or floating-point
rounding) were matched, this was done by comparing outputs, not by reading
its code. ecotraj is not bundled with or required by this package.

Benchmark data: tests/fixtures/ holds ecotraj 1.2.2 outputs computed on
synthetic random inputs, generated by our own scripts in oracle/. No datasets
shipped with ecotraj are included in this repository.

